Angie, there were security cameras.

36
00:04:23,296 --> 00:04:25,338
A new case?

37
00:04:25,339 --> 00:04:30,678
The big score? The mother Iode? The one you've been waiting for?

38
00:04:30,928 --> 00:04:33,980
- Humor me. - Don't I always?

39
00:04:39,042 --> 00:04:42,877
I just pulled a soldier demon out of a little girl.

40
00:04:43,044 --> 00:04:46,756
Looked like it was trying to come through.

41
00:04:47,757 --> 00:04:49,883
Yeah, I know how it sounds.

42
00:04:49,884 --> 00:04:53,346
We're finger puppets to them, John, not doorways.

43
00:04:53,513 --> 00:04:57,474
They can work us, but they can't come through onto our plane.

44
00:04:57,475 --> 00:05:01,938
Check the scrolls anyway. See if there's any precedent.

45
00:05:02,208 --> 00:05:07,211
- That's not the way this works. - Haven't I served him enough?

46
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:11,631
- What does he want from me? - Only the usual.

47
00:05:11,632 --> 00:05:14,217
Self-sacrifice, belief.

48
00:05:14,218 --> 00:05:17,679
- I believe, for Christ's sake. - No, you know.

49
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:20,348
And there's a difference. You've seen.

50
00:05:20,350 --> 00:05:24,561
I never asked to see. I was born with this curse.

51
00:05:24,562 --> 00:05:29,649
A gift, John. One that you've squandered on selfish endeavors.

52
00:05:29,650 --> 00:05:34,572
I'm pulling demons out of little girls. Who's that for?

53
00:05:36,282 --> 00:05:40,285
Everything you've ever done, you've only ever done for yourself.

54
00:05:40,286 --> 00:05:43,079
To earn your way back into his good graces.

55
00:05:43,081 --> 00:05:45,791
Impossible rules, endless regulations...

56
00:05:45,792 --> 00:05:49,128
Who goes up, who goes down and why.

57
00:05:50,748 --> 00:05:53,584
Hey, buddy, got a light?

58
00:06:23,948 --> 00:06:27,993
Should've minded your own business, exorcist.

59
00:06:41,625 --> 00:06:46,001
Not some angry half-breed. A full-fledged demon, on our plane.

60
00:06:46,002 --> 00:06:49,421
Clearly I do not have to remind you that is impossible.

61
00:06:49,422 --> 00:06:51,715
And yesterday I saw a soldier demon

62
00:06:51,716 --> 00:06:55,010
trying to chew its way out through a little girl.

63
00:06:55,011 --> 00:06:58,806
John, demons stay in hell, angels in heaven,

64
00:06:58,807 --> 00:07:02,101
the great détente of the original superpowers.

65
00:07:02,102 --> 00:07:07,566
Thanks for the history lesson, Midnite. You've been a tremendous help.

66
00:07:10,694 --> 00:07:13,113
I need to use the chair.

67
00:07:15,156 --> 00:07:19,994
John, forgetting the fact that it would almost certainly kill you,

68
00:07:19,995 --> 00:07:22,037
you know I am neutral.

69
00:07:22,038 --> 00:07:26,420
And as long as the balance is maintained, I take no sides.

70
00:07:26,458 --> 00:07:29,208
My sister was murdered yesterday.

71
00:07:29,209 --> 00:07:31,795
- Sorry to hear. - Thanks.

72
00:07:32,545 --> 00:07:37,133
She was a patient at Ravenscar. She jumped off the roof.

73
00:07:38,051 --> 00:07:40,469
Thought you said she was murdered.

74
00:07:40,470 --> 00:07:43,555
Isabel wouldn't have taken her own life.

75
00:07:43,556 --> 00:07:47,188
Yeah. What kind of mental patient kills herself? That's just crazy.

76
00:07:47,250 --> 00:07:51,000
Just before my sister was committed, she became deeply paranoid.

77
00:07:51,001 --> 00:07:54,880
She started talking about demons, angels.

78
00:07:55,756 --> 00:07:58,883
Now, I think someone got to her, Mr. Constantine.

79
00:07:58,884 --> 00:08:02,637
I think they brainwashed her into stepping off that roof.

80
00:08:02,638 --> 00:08:05,933
Some kind of legion or cult.

81
00:08:07,309 --> 00:08:11,355
Sounds like a theory, detective. Good luck.

82
00:08:12,042 --> 00:08:14,667
- What? - We should go. Now.

83
00:08:20,506 --> 00:08:23,009
What is that?

84
00:08:23,551 --> 00:08:25,927
Wings.

85
00:08:25,928 --> 00:08:28,389
Maybe talons.

86
00:08:28,514 --> 00:08:31,559
You're kidding. Of what?

87
00:08:32,018 --> 00:08:35,730
Something that's not supposed to be here.

88
00:08:39,233 --> 00:08:42,403
That's really not going to help.

89
00:08:46,407 --> 00:08:49,285
- Close your eyes. - Why?

90
00:08:49,452 --> 00:08:50,706
Suit yourself.

91
00:08:50,831 --> 00:08:53,626
Demons stay in hell, huh?

92
00:08:55,085 --> 00:08:57,421
Tell them that.

93
00:08:59,298 --> 00:09:03,552
Don't worry. Happens to everyone the first time.

94
00:09:04,428 --> 00:09:06,931
It's the sulfur.

95
00:09:07,056 --> 00:09:09,130
Sulfur.

96
00:09:33,563 --> 00:09:36,273
Was it supposed to be hot or cold?

97
00:09:36,274 --> 00:09:38,818
In front of the chair.

98
00:09:41,237 --> 00:09:43,405
I can't believe I'm doing this.

99
00:09:43,406 --> 00:09:46,868
- These are all Isabel's things? - Yeah.

100
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:50,538
- How about the cat? - Duck? Yeah, why?

101
00:09:52,666 --> 00:09:54,458
Duck.

102
00:09:54,459 --> 00:09:58,337
- You think that's strange. - Cats are good.

103
00:09:58,338 --> 00:10:00,176
Half in, half out anyway.

104
00:10:17,426 --> 00:10:19,720
Angela.

105
00:10:21,806 --> 00:10:24,392
Jesus!

106
00:10:27,979 --> 00:10:30,398
- Constantine, what...? - Twins.

107
00:10:30,523 --> 00:10:32,607
What?

108
00:10:32,608 --> 00:10:35,527
- You were twins. - What did you say?

109
00:10:35,528 --> 00:10:38,447
- She killed herself. - What?

110
00:10:39,365 --> 00:10:41,912
And she's damned for it.

111
00:10:41,958 --> 00:10:44,373
How is this possible?

112
00:10:46,125 --> 00:10:48,089
I need to eat.

113
00:10:48,125 --> 00:10:48,412
you find a way out.

114
00:10:48,413 --> 00:10:53,084
- You tried to kill yourself. - I didn't try anything.

115
00:10:55,587 --> 00:10:59,132
Officially, I was dead for two minutes.

116
00:10:59,633 --> 00:11:02,344
But when you cross over,

117
00:11:03,178 --> 00:11:05,722
time stops.

118
00:11:06,848 --> 00:11:11,102
Take it from me, two minutes in hell is a lifetime.

119
00:11:11,770 --> 00:11:14,230
When I came back,

120
00:11:15,857 --> 00:11:20,153
I knew all the things I could see were real.

121
00:11:22,030 --> 00:11:27,118
Heaven and hell are right here. Behind every wall, every window.

122
00:11:27,369 --> 00:11:31,915
The world behind the world, and we're smack in the middle.

123
00:11:32,624 --> 00:11:36,418
Angels and demons can't cross over onto our plane.

124
00:11:36,419 --> 00:11:39,384
So instead we get what I call half-breeds.

125
00:11:39,417 --> 00:11:42,250
I call it hypocritical bullshit.

126
00:11:43,876 --> 00:11:47,087
So when a half-breed breaks the rules,

127
00:11:47,088 --> 00:11:51,342
I deport their sorry ass straight back to hell.

128
00:11:51,676 --> 00:11:53,928
I don't get them all,

129
00:11:54,929 --> 00:11:59,309
but I've been hoping to get enough to ensure my...

130
00:11:59,767 --> 00:12:03,021
- Retirement. - I don't understand.

131
00:12:04,564 --> 00:12:06,982
I'm a suicide, Angela.

132
00:12:06,983 --> 00:12:10,652
When I die, the rules say I've got just one place to go.

133
00:12:10,792 --> 00:12:15,626
Maybe she left something else. Not something a cop would find.

134
00:12:17,503 --> 00:12:19,964
Something just for you.

135
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:25,177
You were her twin, Angela. Twins tend to think alike.

136
00:12:25,178 --> 00:12:28,847
- I'm not like my sister. - But you were once.

137
00:12:28,848 --> 00:12:34,060
When you were kids. When you'd spend every second with each other.

138
00:12:34,061 --> 00:12:38,231
You'd start a sentence, she'd finish it. You'd get hurt, she'd cry.

139
00:12:38,232 --> 00:12:41,943
- That was a long time ago. - That kind of bond doesn't disappear.

140
00:12:41,944 --> 00:12:44,075
There is nothing here.

141
00:12:44,125 --> 00:12:46,665
When we were girls,

142
00:12:48,542 --> 00:12:52,046
we would leave each other messages.

143
00:12:54,632 --> 00:12:56,967
In light.

144
00:12:59,053 --> 00:13:01,555
In breath.

145
00:13:05,309 --> 00:13:07,561
On the windows.

146
00:13:10,458 --> 00:13:14,874
"The sins of the father would only be exceeded by the sins of the son."

147
00:13:14,875 --> 00:13:18,336
- Whose son? - But he can't cross over, B.

148
00:13:18,337 --> 00:13:21,339
- Impossible to cross over. - Whose son? God's son?

149
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:25,010
No, the other one. Devil had a son too.

150
00:13:25,135 --> 00:13:26,844
Here it is.

151
00:13:26,845 --> 00:13:30,766
This is the sign of Mammon, the son of the devil.

152
00:13:31,016 --> 00:13:33,648
Hold on, it says here...

153
00:13:33,788 --> 00:13:37,582
No, wait, wait, wait. I'm reading. Seems to be a loophole.

154
00:13:37,583 --> 00:13:39,919
Always a catch.

155
00:13:40,127 --> 00:13:45,841
It says first Mammon would have to possess a very, very powerful psychic.

156
00:13:46,717 --> 00:13:49,929
- Isabel. - But that wouldn 't be enough.

157
00:13:50,054 --> 00:13:54,392
To cross over, Mammon would need divine assistance.

158
00:13:55,768 --> 00:13:59,981
To cross over, Mammon would need the help of God.

159
00:14:00,167 --> 00:14:02,915
- Beeman? - John, look...

160
00:14:03,583 --> 00:14:08,169
I know you've never had much faith, you've never had much reason to...

161
00:14:08,170 --> 00:14:12,757
But that doesn't mean that we don't have faith

162
00:14:12,758 --> 00:14:15,428
in you.

163
00:14:17,888 --> 00:14:20,182
Beeman?

164
00:14:21,225 --> 00:14:23,588
Drive. Fast.

165
00:14:39,917 --> 00:14:42,082
Beeman!

166
00:14:42,207 --> 00:14:44,793
Sulfur.

167
00:14:45,168 --> 00:14:47,462
Beeman!

168
00:14:51,257 --> 00:14:52,930
Beeman!

169
00:14:52,958 --> 00:14:53,870
By the time we were 10, they started forcing her to take antipsychotics

170
00:14:53,871 --> 00:14:56,915
and have treatments.

171
00:14:56,916 --> 00:15:02,505
They would come for her and she'd look at me, and she'd say to me, "Tell them."

172
00:15:02,755 --> 00:15:07,176
"Why don't you tell them, Angie, that you can see them too?"

173
00:15:07,843 --> 00:15:09,928
But I lied.

174
00:15:09,929 --> 00:15:12,139
I said:

175
00:15:13,057 --> 00:15:15,768
"I don't see anything."

176
00:15:16,685 --> 00:15:19,230
Until one day,

177
00:15:19,939 --> 00:15:22,942
I finally stopped seeing.

178
00:15:24,026 --> 00:15:26,779
I abandoned her, John.

179
00:15:27,279 --> 00:15:29,990
I left her all alone.

180
00:15:36,872 --> 00:15:39,416
I need to see what she saw.

181
00:15:41,417 --> 00:15:44,874
You do this, there's no turning back.

182
00:15:46,876 --> 00:15:49,671
You see them,

183
00:15:49,796 --> 00:15:52,048
they see you.

184
00:15:52,632 --> 00:15:55,135
Understand?

185
00:15:55,426 --> 00:15:57,183
Yeah.

186
00:15:57,250 --> 00:16:01,208
Normally, only a portion of the body has to be suspended,

187
00:16:04,044 --> 00:16:06,379
but you wanted the crash course.

188
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:09,257
Yeah, I wanted the crash course.

189
00:16:09,258 --> 00:16:13,971
- So, what's gonna happen? - Lie down.

190
00:16:15,806 --> 00:16:20,727
- What do you mean lie down? - You have to be fully submerged.

191
00:16:21,562 --> 00:16:24,940
- For how long? - As long as it takes.

192
00:16:35,617 --> 00:16:37,874
Take a deep one.

193
00:16:37,917 --> 00:16:40,248
God.

194
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:43,709
God, all those people.

195
00:16:44,669 --> 00:16:47,296
Isabel!

196
00:16:47,505 --> 00:16:50,757
I've always known. I've always known where they are.

197
00:16:50,758 --> 00:16:53,343
I've always known where to find them,

198
00:16:53,344 --> 00:16:56,513
where to aim and where to duck

199
00:16:56,514 --> 00:16:59,015
and I've always known where they were.

200
00:16:59,016 --> 00:17:02,478
I've always known that it wasn't luck.

201
00:17:02,603 --> 00:17:06,440
I've always known that I could see.

202
00:17:07,024 --> 00:17:10,736
I've always known that I could see.

203
00:17:41,315 --> 00:17:43,942
It was his.

204
00:17:43,943 --> 00:17:46,571
Rolling.

205
00:17:47,947 --> 00:17:50,491
Not a ball.

206
00:17:51,451 --> 00:17:54,120
Something smaller.

207
00:17:55,872 --> 00:17:58,087
Shiny.

208
00:17:58,125 --> 00:18:00,378
Balthazar.

209
00:18:00,495 --> 00:18:03,122
Fire? I was born of this.

210
00:18:03,748 --> 00:18:08,378
How's Mammon crossing over, you half-breed piece of shit?

211
00:18:11,923 --> 00:18:14,801
That's better. Au naturel.

212
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:26,020
"Stay in the car, wait here."

213
00:18:28,272 --> 00:18:29,529
Men.

214
00:18:29,583 --> 00:18:31,579
Not really, no.

215
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:36,502
You can't cheat it this time. You're going back to hell.

216
00:18:36,669 --> 00:18:39,004
True, but you're not.

217
00:18:41,006 --> 00:18:44,509
- What are you doing? - I'm reading you your last rites.

218
00:18:44,510 --> 00:18:48,012
Spare me your remedial incantations.

219
00:18:48,013 --> 00:18:50,932
You do know what it is to truly be forgiven?

220
00:18:50,933 --> 00:18:54,185
To be welcomed into the Kingdom of God.

221
00:18:54,186 --> 00:18:56,771
Demon in heaven.

222
00:18:56,772 --> 00:18:59,733
I'd love to be a fly on that wall.

223
00:18:59,858 --> 00:19:03,445
You're not a priest. You have no power.

224
00:19:04,863 --> 00:19:07,615
Just tell me how Mammon is crossing over

225
00:19:07,616 --> 00:19:10,911
and you can go back to your shithole.

226
